  "discussion": "Broadly, the risk management framework defined by the [Information security manual](https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/asds-cyber-security-frameworks/ism) has six steps: define the system, select security controls, implement security controls, assess security controls, authorise the system and monitor the system. System owners are responsible for the implementation of this six-step risk management framework for each of their systems.",
